<title>MEXICO: Telmex shareholders approve stock buyback.</title>
<headline>Telmex shareholders approve stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telefonos de Mexico, S.A. (Telmex) said Wednesday its shareholders had approved a plan that allows the company to repurchase up to 800 million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;They approved increasing the reserve for repurchasing the shares up to an amount of 14,232.6 million pesos...the company could obtain up to a maximum of 800 million of said shares,&quot; the telephone company said in a statement from the Mexican stock exchange.</p>
<p>The decision was approved by shareholders at a special general meeting on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Cecilia Cardenas, Mexico City Newsroom (525) 728 9552</p>
